ing a real restart. After reboot, findmnt confirmed both /tmp and /dev/shm mounted with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec, and the functional execution-denial tests were re-run and passed, proving the hardening survives reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected current mount state, fstab, and tmp.mount unit on node1\",\"Backed up /etc/fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec\",\"Ran systemctl daemon-reload and remounted /tmp and /dev/shm live\",\"Verified noexec/nosuid/nodev enforcement via functional tests (script execution denied)\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and mount state before restart\",\"Rebooted node1 via systemctl reboot (backgrounded so acknowledgement returned first)\",\"Polled node1 until it became reachable again\",\"Verified boot_id changed, confirming a genuine restart\",\"Re-verified /tmp and /dev/shm mount options and functional enforcement post-reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline mount/fstab state before change\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-051384ae1b044191\",\"cmd-854e6aeb26a449fc\"],\"summary\":\"Showed /tmp was not separately mounted (part of root xfs), /dev/shm was tmpfs without noexec, and no fstab entries existed for either, plus tmp.mount unit was disabled.\"},{\"requirement\":\"fstab updated with noexec,nosuid,nodev for /tmp and /dev/shm\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-291d184904cc4602\"],\"summary\":\"Backed up fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec, confirmed via cat /etc/fstab.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mounts applied live and options confirmed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-75567d5d8ca74368\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl daemon-reload plus mount/remount applied the new options immediately; findmnt showed both /tmp and /dev/shm with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Functional proof execution/setuid/device are ignored before reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a4ab5554c8bd49f9\",\"cmd-08d8b645c34c4128\"],\"summary\":\"Executable scripts placed in /tmp and /dev/shm failed with Permission denied (exit 126) due to noexec; test artifacts cleaned up.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart baseline boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9641787808664d81\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 98aa35f5-6905-42fd-9f07-0e28f75b4fa6 and confirmed mount options were healthy immediately before restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5e520cfa45974122\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded systemctl reboot with a short delay so the exec call returned successfully (reboot scheduled, pid=1628) before the node went down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node unreachable during reboot, then proof of changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d3a3e7eb14834630\",\"cmd-d9bfa61dc02745ba\",\"cmd-be8c256794b74cc0\",\"cmd-1ea766be3d1d44c4\"],\"summary\":\"Polling showed the node still up briefly, then connection timeouts during the reboot window, then a successful reconnect with a new boot_id (662e94b4-e11c-440a-a86d-d699717075e9), proving an actual restart occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery and persistence of hardened mounts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a4a7ed60c1e74d02\",\"cmd-726b83ffc1994db9\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, findmnt confirmed /tmp and /dev/shm still mounted with nosuid,nodev,noexec, and functional execution tests again failed with Permission denied, proving the hardening survived the restart.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, /etc/fstab was updated to add tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec. Both were remounted live and verified to enforce noexec/nosuid/nodev via functional tests (script execution denied on both). Node1 was then rebooted using systemctl reboot; boot_id changed from 98aa35f5-6905-42fd-9f07-0e28f75b4fa6 to 662e94b4-e11c-440a-a86d-d699717075e9, confirming a real restart. After reboot, findmnt confirmed both /tmp and /dev/shm mounted with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec, and the functional execution-denial tests were re-run and passed, proving the hardening survives reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected current mount state, fstab, and tmp.mount unit on node1","Backed up /etc/fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec","Ran systemctl daemon-reload and remounted /tmp and /dev/shm live","Verified noexec/nosuid/nodev enforcement via functional tests (script execution denied)","Captured baseline boot_id and mount state before restart","Rebooted node1 via systemctl reboot (backgrounded so acknowledgement returned first)","Polled node1 until it became reachable again","Verified boot_id changed, confirming a genuine restart","Re-verified /tmp and /dev/shm mount options and functional enforcement post-reboot"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline mount/fstab state before change","command_ids":["cmd-051384ae1b044191","cmd-854e6aeb26a449fc"],"summary":"Showed /tmp was not separately mounted (part of root xfs), /dev/shm was tmpfs without noexec, and no fstab entries existed for either, plus tmp.mount unit was disabled."},{"requirement":"fstab updated with noexec,nosuid,nodev for /tmp and /dev/shm","command_ids":["cmd-291d184904cc4602"],"summary":"Backed up fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec, confirmed via cat /etc/fstab."},{"requirement":"Mounts applied live and options confirmed","command_ids":["cmd-75567d5d8ca74368"],"summary":"systemctl daemon-reload plus mount/remount applied the new options immediately; findmnt showed both /tmp and /dev/shm with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec."},{"requirement":"Functional proof execution/setuid/device are ignored before reboot","command_ids":["cmd-a4ab5554c8bd49f9","cmd-08d8b645c34c4128"],"summary":"Executable scripts placed in /tmp and /dev/shm failed with Permission denied (exit 126) due to noexec; test artifacts cleaned up."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart baseline boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-9641787808664d81"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 98aa35f5-6905-42fd-9f07-0e28f75b4fa6 and confirmed mount options were healthy immediately before restart."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-5e520cfa45974122"],"summary":"Backgrounded systemctl reboot with a short delay so the exec call returned successfully (reboot scheduled, pid=1628) before the node went down."},{"requirement":"Node unreachable during reboot, then proof of changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-d3a3e7eb14834630","cmd-d9bfa61dc02745ba","cmd-be8c256794b74cc0","cmd-1ea766be3d1d44c4"],"summary":"Polling showed the node still up briefly, then connection timeouts during the reboot window, then a successful reconnect with a new boot_id (662e94b4-e11c-440a-a86d-d699717075e9), proving an actual restart occurred."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery and persistence of hardened mounts","command_ids":["cmd-a4a7ed60c1e74d02","cmd-726b83ffc1994db9"],"summary":"After reboot, findmnt confirmed /tmp and /dev/shm still mounted with nosuid,nodev,noexec, and functional execution tests again failed with Permission denied, proving the hardening survived the restart."}]},"ttft_ms":1618,"type":"result","duration_ms":59338,"uuid":"34745b09-0fdd-4b33-8a33-72aed8149bea","ttft_stream_ms":657,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":657,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
